  "title": "Kirby Problem 2.6",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Give a classification or enumeration of the finite-index sub-\ngroups of $\\operatorname{Mod}(S_{g})$ that are generated by Dehn twists, Dehn multitwists, or powers\nthereof. Which of these subgroups are “geometrically meaningful”, in the sense that\nthey are given as the stabilizers of some kind of geometric or topological struc-\nture on the surface? Conversely, when is a geometrically meaningful subgroup (not\nnecessarily of finite index) generated by powers of Dehn multitwists?",
